WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.810
Adipose tissue is active tissue.

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:06.045
White adipose stores excess
energy as triglycerides and acts

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.140
as an endocrine organ.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:12.320
Its adipokines participate in
energy balance, insulin sensitivity, and

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.596
inflammatory responses.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.816
Watch the stored fat
expand within the illustrated cells.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.522
Brown adipose is rich in mitochondria.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.880
Cold exposure and sympathetic
activation can stimulate it to

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.840
generate heat through uncoupling protein one.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.880
Beige tissue can emerge
within white adipose with chronic

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.940
cold exposure or exercise.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.260
With warm adaptation, beige tissue can return to white

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:34.869
adipose.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.040
In obesity, macrophages infiltrate
adipose tissue and inflammatory mediators

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:40.520
are released.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.140
The supplied slides connect
these changes with possible insulin

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:44.650
resistance.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:48.763
More stored fat, altered
endocrine signals, and inflammation belong

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.920
to the same mechanism.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.189
Fat storage and heat
production are different functions.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.793
Keep white, brown, and beige adipose distinct.
